# PRO features

Thirteen features, each in its own folder, each behind its own flag in
`Config/FeatureFlags.swift`. **All default to `false`**; `setup.sh` writes the
buyer's choices into the `featureFlags:` line of `AppConfig.swift`.

| Feature | Folder | Flag |
|---|---|---|
| AI PRO — streaming chat + history | `Modules/AIPro` | `aiPro` |
| Widgets + Live Activities | `Widgets/` | `widgets` |
| Gamification (XP, levels, badges, streaks) | `Modules/Gamification` | `gamification` |
| Quiz / questionnaire onboarding | `Modules/QuestionnaireOnboarding` | `questionnaireOnboarding` |
| Camera + document scanner + OCR | `Modules/Capture` | `camera` |
| Local reminders | `Modules/Reminders` | `reminders` |
| SwiftData offline store | `Modules/SwiftDataStore` | `swiftDataStore` |
| 10 paywall templates + gallery | `Modules/PaywallTemplates` | `paywallTemplates` |
| Swift Charts demos | `Modules/Charts` | `charts` |
| In-app feedback | `Modules/Feedback` | `inAppFeedback` |
| Biometric app lock | `Modules/AppLock` | `biometricLock` |
| Runtime localization (en/es/hi) | `Modules/Localization` | `localization` |
| App Store review prompt | `Modules/Review` | `reviewPrompt` |

## Where each one is surfaced — get this right

| Surface | Reachable features |
|---|---|
| `Modules/Demo/TestDriveView.swift` **(`#if DEBUG` only)** | charts · paywallTemplates · gamification · reminders · swiftDataStore · camera · aiPro · widgets · questionnaireOnboarding · localization · inAppFeedback · app-lock test |
| `Modules/Settings/SettingsView.swift` **(ships in Release)** | `biometricLock` toggle · `localization` picker · `inAppFeedback` form · `reviewPrompt` button |
| Root modifier in `TheSwiftKitApp` | `biometricLock` overlay (`.appLockGate`) · `localization` (`\.locale` + `.id`) |

**In a Release build, nine of the thirteen have no entry point.** That is by
design — they are reference implementations the buyer wires into their own
product, not shipped screens. **Do not add them to `HomeView`, `RootView` or
`AppRoute`** unless explicitly asked; that would put demo content in every
buyer's shipping app.

## The removal contract

A buyer must be able to remove any Pro feature in two steps:

1. Flip its flag to `false`.
2. Delete its folder.

For that to hold, **nothing outside a feature's folder may reference its types**
— except these audited shared files, which are the only legitimate touch points:

- `Config/FeatureFlags.swift` (the flag)
- `Modules/Settings/SettingsView.swift` (the four Release-reachable features)
- `Modules/Demo/TestDriveView.swift` (the DEBUG hub)
- `Core/Root/TheSwiftKitApp.swift` (`.appLockGate`, `\.locale`, `.id(...)`)
- `project.yml` (widget target, `Widgets/Shared`, Info.plist keys)
- `Resources/*.lproj/Localizable.strings` (the feature's keys)

**Re-check this list whenever you touch a Pro feature.** If a change makes a
shared file fail to compile after deleting the folder, wrap it or move it.

## Pro managers are singletons — deliberately

```
AppLockManager.shared      LocalizationManager.shared   ReviewManager.shared
GamificationEngine.shared  ReminderScheduler.shared
```

All `@MainActor final class … : ObservableObject`. This breaks the base rule
("no singletons, use `DIContainer`") **on purpose**: a `DIContainer` property
referencing a Pro type would stop the project compiling the moment a buyer
deleted that folder. A `.shared` inside the folder disappears with it.

**Follow this for new Pro features. Never add a Pro service to `DIContainer`.**
For core (non-Pro) services the base rule still applies.

## Per-feature gotchas

- **`biometricLock` is two-condition:** the flag makes it *available*; the user
  still opts in via the Settings toggle persisted as `appLockEnabled`. Both must
  be true before the lock screen appears. Needs `NSFaceIDUsageDescription`.
- **`swiftDataStore` is `@available(iOS 17, *)`** in an iOS 16 project — keep
  the availability gate on every entry point you add.
- **`charts`** needs no gate (Swift Charts is iOS 16+).
- **`camera`** needs `NSCameraUsageDescription`; uses VisionKit
  (`DocumentScannerView`) + Vision (`TextRecognizer`).
- **`widgets`** is a separate target (`TheSwiftKitWidgets`, iOS **16.1**+,
  bundle id `<app>.widgets`). `Widgets/Shared` compiles into **both** app and
  extension — keep it free of app-only dependencies. Widgets currently render
  **sample data**; sharing real data needs an App Group, which is *not*
  configured (no entitlement, no suite name — see the TODO in
  `Widgets/TheSwiftKitWidgets.swift`).
- **`aiPro`** streams from `/v1/chat/stream` (SSE) and falls back to a built-in
  canned streamer when the backend is unreachable. **Keep that fallback** — it
  is what makes the demo work out of the box.
- **`paywallTemplates`** (`Template01…Template10`) use `DS` tokens and shared
  `PaywallComponents` — they are not a parallel styling system. A `DS` retheme
  restyles all ten.
- **`localization`** ships `Base`/`en`/`es`/`hi`. Adding a language means a new
  `<code>.lproj/Localizable.strings`, a row in `LocalizationManager.supported`,
  and the code in `CFBundleLocalizations` in `project.yml`.

## Adding a new Pro feature

1. Create `Modules/MyProFeature/` — everything for it lives here.
2. Add a flag to `FeatureFlags.swift` (default `false`) **and to `setup.sh`**,
   which rewrites the whole `featureFlags:` line and will otherwise drop it.
3. Use a `@MainActor` `.shared` manager if it needs state — not `DIContainer`.
4. Surface it from `TestDriveView` (and `SettingsView` only if it should ship in
   Release).
5. Add localization keys to all four `.lproj` files.
6. Add any Info.plist usage strings to `project.yml`, commented with the feature
   they belong to.
7. Verify the removal contract: flag off + folder deleted must still compile.
8. `xcodegen generate`.
